the trooper cabra a mysterious creature  common in Latin American folklore with  its first sightings been reported in  Puerto Rico during the mid 90s the  chupacabra developed the reputation when  livestock began mysteriously dying the  animals were found completely drained of  blood  through a small circular fang-like  incision according to experts at the  time these incisions could not be from  any known animal of the region there  were more than 200 reports of the  chupacabra being seen in 1995 alone  the creature became an urban legend all  over South America but as quickly as  these sightings began they stopped with  no trace leaving a host of questions the  named trooper cabra translated in  Spanish roughly means goat sucker  referring to how the creature attacks  its prey  the appearance of the chupacabra varies  drastically some claim the animal is the  size of a small bear and others believe  it is no bigger than a wolf in most  depictions it has rows of spines that  run from the base of its neck to its  tail the Beast has razor-sharp teeth or  vampire-like fangs  along with draining the blood of its  victims it is sometimes depicted as  having wings similar to that of a bat  meaning that people consider the  chupacabra to be a vampire like beasts  there have been claims from local  villages that the trooper cabra is a  large reptilian like creature who is  able to walk on two legs as the  chupacabra has become such a widespread  legend there are varying reports of the  creature strengths and weaknesses the  chupacabras bite contains a strong venom  allowing them to stun their victims  while they feed on them its bites may  even be considered contagious in fact in  anyone its fangs come into contact with  turning them into a chupacabra  the chupacabra can overpower large  animals and even sometimes humans rip in  their flesh from their bones with ease  there are reports that claim the  chupacabra has the ability of hypnosis  it is believed that anything that stares  into its red eyes will become paralyzed  leaving them motionless while the  Chupacabra feeds thanks to its wings and  web joints the creature is able to glide  long distances make an escape for its  prey almost impossible despite its vast  array of strengths there are ways to  kill a chupacabra many believe much like  a vampire  the chupacabra has a strong aversion to  the Sun meaning that direct sunlight  will kill the creature it is also  believed that guns can harm the  chupacabra  with the shotgun being preferred as the  wide spread of the buckshot makes it  impossible for the chupacabra to  regenerate similar to sunlight fire can  burn the chupacabra and is thought to be  a useful tool and trying to repel the  Beast  there were many conspiracy theories as  to where the chupacabra came from the  most popular being that it was  engineered in the lab by NASA when  experimenting on guerrillas in Chile  NASA quickly denied this theory  comparing it to that of the fake moon  landing conspiracy even with most of the  trooper Cobra attacks being explained as  a breed of wild dog there are people who  believe that it was something else  if you've enjoyed this video then please  go ahead and leave it a like consider  subscribing if folklore mythology is  something that interests you if you have  anything you'd like to discuss or have  any ideas for future videos then please  go ahead and let me know in the comments  below as always I've been your host  mythology and folklore explained
 

